# Test Driven Development (TDD) Guidelines

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này định nghĩa các nguyên tắc và best practices cho việc implement Test Driven Development (TDD) trong Cursor Enterprise Framework. Mục tiêu là đảm bảo code quality, better design, faster development, và maintainable codebase thông qua test-first approach.

TDD là discipline viết tests trước khi viết code, với cycle: Red (viết test fail) → Green (viết code pass) → Refactor (cải thiện code). Việc tuân thủ TDD mang lại confidence trong code changes và better design decisions.

## Nguyên tắc cơ bản

### 1. TDD Cycle

Understanding the red-green-refactor cycle.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      TDD Cycle                                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                  │
│  1. RED Phase                                                   │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Write a failing test that describes the desired         │   │
│  │  behavior. The test should fail for the right reason.    │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│  2. GREEN Phase                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Write the minimum code necessary to make the test       │   │
│  │  pass. Don't worry about perfect code, just make it      │   │
│  │  work.                                                   │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│  3. REFACTOR Phase                                             │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Improve the code while keeping tests passing.           │   │
│  │  Remove duplication, improve naming, simplify logic.     │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│                         Repeat...                                │
│                                                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2. Test Naming Conventions

Consistent và descriptive test names.

```typescript
// Test naming pattern: describe + it
describe('OrderAggregate', () => {
    describe('addItem', () => {
        it('should add item to draft order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should throw error when adding item to confirmed order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should not add zero quantity items', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });
    });

    describe('confirm', () => {
        it('should confirm order with items and valid payment', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should throw error when confirming empty order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should throw error when order is already confirmed', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });
    });
});

// BDD-style naming
describe('Order Creation', () => {
    scenario('customer can create order with valid items', () => {
        given('a customer with valid cart items');
        when('they submit order');
        then('order should be created with status DRAFT');
    });

    scenario('customer cannot create empty order', () => {
        given('a customer with empty cart');
        when('they submit order');
        then('error should be returned');
    });
});

// Test categories
describe('Unit Tests', () => {});
describe('Integration Tests', () => {});
describe('E2E Tests', () => {});
```

### 3. Arrange-Act-Assert Pattern

Structure tests clearly.

```typescript
// Classic AAA pattern
describe('OrderService', () => {
    describe('createOrder', () => {
        it('should create order successfully with valid input', async () => {
            // Arrange
            const customerId = 'cust-123';
            const input = {
                customerId,
                items: [
                    { productId: 'prod-1', quantity: 2 },
                    { productId: 'prod-2', quantity: 1 }
                ],
                shippingAddress: testAddress()
            };

            mockRepository.findById.mockResolvedValue(null);
            mockPaymentGateway.charge.mockResolvedValue({
                success: true,
                paymentId: 'pay-123'
            });

            // Act
            const result = await service.createOrder(input);

            // Assert
            expect(result).toBeDefined();
            expect(result.id).toBeDefined();
            expect(result.status).toBe('CONFIRMED');
            expect(mockRepository.save).toHaveBeenCalled();
            expect(mockPaymentGateway.charge).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
                expect.objectContaining({
                    orderId: expect.any(String),
                    amount: expect.any(Number)
                })
            );
        });

        it('should throw PaymentFailedException when payment fails', async () => {
            // Arrange
            mockPaymentGateway.charge.mockResolvedValue({
                success: false,
                error: 'Card declined'
            });

            // Act & Assert
            await expect(service.createOrder(testInput()))
                .rejects.toThrow(PaymentFailedException);

            expect(mockRepository.save).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
        });
    });
});
```

### 4. Test Isolation

Keep tests independent.

```typescript
// Bad - test dependency
describe('OrderTests', () => {
    let order: Order;

    beforeAll(() => {
        // This creates shared state!
        order = createGlobalOrder();
    });

    it('should add item', () => {
        order.addItem(testProduct(), 2);
        expect(order.items.length).toBe(1);  // Depends on previous test!
    });
});

// Good - isolated tests
describe('OrderTests', () => {
    it('should add item to empty order', () => {
        const order = createDraftOrder();  // Fresh instance
        order.addItem(testProduct(), 2);
        expect(order.items.length).toBe(1);
    });

    it('should add multiple items', () => {
        const order = createDraftOrder();  // Fresh instance
        order.addItem(testProduct('A'), 2);
        order.addItem(testProduct('B'), 1);
        expect(order.items.length).toBe(2);
    });

    it('should calculate correct total', () => {
        const order = createDraftOrder();
        order.addItem(testProduct('A', 100), 2);  // 200
        order.addItem(testProduct('B', 50), 1);   // 50
        expect(order.total.amount).toBe(250);
    });
});

// Factory functions for test setup
function createDraftOrder(): Order {
    return Order.create(
        new CustomerId('test-customer'),
        testAddress()
    );
}

function testProduct(name = 'Test Product', price = 100): Product {
    return new Product(
        new ProductId('prod-' + Math.random()),
        new ProductName(name),
        Money.fromDecimal(price, Currency.USD)
    );
}
```

### 5. Test Coverage Strategy

Cover critical paths.

```typescript
// Test coverage pyramid
/*
                    ┌──────────────┐
                    │     E2E      │  5-10% (few, critical flows)
                    │    Tests     │
                    ├──────────────┤
                    │  Integration │  20-30% (API, DB interactions)
                    │    Tests     │
                    ├──────────────┤
                    │   Unit       │  60-70% (business logic)
                    │   Tests      │
                    └──────────────┘
*/

// Coverage by category
describe('Domain Layer - 100% coverage', () => {
    // Entities
    // Value Objects
    // Aggregates
    // Domain Services
});

describe('Application Layer - 90% coverage', () => {
    // Use Cases
    // Application Services
    // DTOs
});

describe('Infrastructure Layer - 70% coverage', () => {
    // Repository implementations
    // External service adapters
});

// Critical path coverage
describe('Critical Paths', () => {
    it('order creation flow', () => { /* ... */ });
    it('payment processing flow', () => { /* ... */ });
    it('order cancellation flow', () => { /* ... */ });
    it('refund processing flow', () => { /* ... */ });
});
```

### 6. Mocking Best Practices

Use mocks appropriately.

```typescript
// Mock only external dependencies
describe('OrderService', () => {
    let service: OrderService;
    let mockRepository: jest.Mocked<IOrderRepository>;
    let mockPaymentGateway: jest.Mocked<IPaymentGateway>;

    beforeEach(() => {
        // Create mocks for external dependencies
        mockRepository = {
            save: jest.fn(),
            findById: jest.fn(),
            findByCustomer: jest.fn()
        };

        mockPaymentGateway = {
            charge: jest.fn(),
            refund: jest.fn()
        };

        service = new OrderService(mockRepository, mockPaymentGateway);
    });

    // Don't mock domain objects - use real instances
    it('should process order correctly', () => {
        const realOrder = Order.create(testCustomerId(), testAddress());

        mockPaymentGateway.charge.mockResolvedValue({
            success: true,
            paymentId: 'pay-123'
        });

        service.processOrder(realOrder);

        expect(realOrder.status).toBe(OrderStatus.CONFIRMED);
    });
});

// Mock libraries
const mockLogger = {
    info: jest.fn(),
    error: jest.fn(),
    warn: jest.fn()
};

// Use spy for partial mocking
it('should call repository save', async () => {
    const saveSpy = jest.spyOn(repository, 'save');

    await service.createOrder(testInput());

    expect(saveSpy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
});
```

### 7. Edge Case Testing

Test boundary conditions.

```typescript
describe('Quantity validation', () => {
    it('should reject zero quantity', () => {
        expect(() => new Quantity(0)).toThrow(ValidationException);
    });

    it('should reject negative quantity', () => {
        expect(() => new Quantity(-1)).toThrow(ValidationException);
    });

    it('should accept minimum valid quantity', () => {
        const q = new Quantity(1);
        expect(q.value).toBe(1);
    });

    it('should accept maximum valid quantity', () => {
        const q = new Quantity(9999);
        expect(q.value).toBe(9999);
    });
});

describe('Money operations', () => {
    it('should handle zero money', () => {
        const zero = Money.zero(Currency.USD);
        const amount = Money.fromDecimal(100, Currency.USD);

        const result = zero.add(amount);
        expect(result.amount).toBe(100);
    });

    it('should handle currency mismatch', () => {
        const usd = Money.fromDecimal(100, Currency.USD);
        const eur = Money.fromDecimal(100, Currency.EUR);

        expect(() => usd.add(eur)).toThrow(CurrencyMismatchException);
    });

    it('should handle large amounts', () => {
        const amount = Money.fromDecimal(999999999.99, Currency.USD);
        expect(amount.amount).toBe(999999999.99);
    });
});

describe('Order status transitions', () => {
    it('should allow DRAFT -> CONFIRMED', () => {
        const order = createDraftOrder();
        expect(() => order.confirm('pay-123')).not.toThrow();
    });

    it('should allow CONFIRMED -> SHIPPED', () => {
        const order = createConfirmedOrder();
        expect(() => order.ship()).not.toThrow();
    });

    it('should allow CONFIRMED -> CANCELLED', () => {
        const order = createConfirmedOrder();
        expect(() => order.cancel('Customer request')).not.toThrow();
    });

    it('should not allow SHIPPED -> CANCELLED', () => {
        const order = createShippedOrder();
        expect(() => order.cancel('Customer request')).toThrow(InvalidTransitionException);
    });
});
```

